	I agree, using the Riftwar series as a point of reference, they tell
	us that Elven arrows (or is it bows) doesn't really matter, increase 
	even a humans skill since part of the elven magic goes into the work.

>It seems strange to me that a crossbow should do the same amount
>of damage as other bows; don't they shoot much harder?

	Not really that strange, crossbows lose their effectiveness with 
	distance. Alot of the resulting damage of the crossbow is the shock 
	associated with the blow.

	The best way to deal with this would be to have the missile weapons 
	have varying damage according to the distance away from the target. 
	Crossbows would inflict the most damage at an optimal distance of 
	say 2 but would be less likely of a hit since the prey would be more
	aware of them while the Long Bow would be effective at 6 with a
	greater chance of a hit, but with a less damage due to the distance.
	The damage and likelihood of a hit would depend upon the character,
	and the distance.

